  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "One game, thirteen complete worlds",
    "overview": "Afterblock keeps the board and thumb controls dominant while each selectable theme carries a complete material treatment through menus, sheets, the board and piece previews. The user approved all nine new worlds alongside the four existing themes. This is a family of visual systems rather than a single palette with interchangeable accent colors.\n\nThe theme registry and stylesheet are the authority for exact appearance; the Canvas renderer is the authority for tiles and ghosts. Short functional English labels, locally bundled typefaces for the new worlds and a shared phone-first geometry keep the experience coherent. Theme changes alter appearance without moving gameplay controls.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Thirteen complete shell and board palettes.",
      "Nine new worlds with local type, distinct corners and Canvas materials.",
      "Shared safe areas, compact status rows and configurable translucent controls.",
      "Static pattern identities in Movement Score, Data Field and LCD."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Complete World Rule",
        "body": "Switch the full shell and Canvas palette together; do not leave tokens from the previous theme behind.",
        "section": "colors"
